WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.700
A balance reads to two
decimal places of a gram.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.460
Weigh out 5.00 grams
of a solid on it.

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:12.920
Now weigh out a tiny pinch:
just 0.10 grams.

4
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.100
Same balance.

5
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.940
Same care each time.

6
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.880
Yet chemists trust the first
result far more than the second.

7
00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.880
Why does weighing a tiny amount
make the result less trustworthy?

8
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.000
In this mission, you'll see
why no measurement is exact,

9
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.380
and tell an accurate
result from a precise one.

10
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.360
Then you'll sort random
errors from systematic ones,

11
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.040
and round answers to the right
number of significant figures.

12
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.720
Your mission: explain why a tiny amount
gives a less trustworthy result.